description: 'v031''s exact recipe at 8 epochs instead of 3. 225,922 params, hidden
  128, input_proj 64, distill_weight 2.0. The composition test: both levers that have
  ever worked.'
hypothesis: "Two things have moved this model: distillation weight (v031, +5.5 sigma)\
  \ and training length (v032, +4.5 sigma for 5 epochs over 3). Both are single scalars\
  \ and both were measured at the OTHER lever's default. This asks whether they compose.\n\
  \n  If they do, the prediction is additive -- v031's 0.687376 plus v032's +0.000708\
  \ gives about 0.6881 local. If they interact, one may be partly redundant, since\
  \ both plausibly act by sharpening the fit to the teacher and doubling both could\
  \ saturate rather than add.\n\n  There is a second reason to prefer a long schedule\
  \ that has nothing to do with the local number. v025 and v032 are both 5-epoch runs\
  \ and v025 carried an OFFSET 0.0024 better than the 3-epoch band, a shift in the\
  \ local-to-public mapping that local validation is structurally incapable of seeing.\
  \ v032 was built to settle that and is packaged but not yet submitted. Longer training\
  \ has now twice moved something local cannot observe, so the local component here\
  \ is the smaller half of the question.\n\n  dozken's own best recipes ran 10 epochs\
  \ and he reports the distilled model peaking at epoch 3 and declining after, so\
  \ over-training is a real failure mode here -- which is why 8 rather than 12."
change_vs_parent: training.epochs 3 -> 8 only. Everything else identical to v031.
